  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#update-the-rendering filters documents just once in step 3:\n\n>  Filter non-renderable documents: Remove from docs any [Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#document) object doc for which any of the following are true:\n> - doc is [render-blocked](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#render-blocked);\n> - doc's [visibility state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#visibility-state) is \"hidden\";\n> - doc's rendering is [suppressed for view transitions](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-view-transitions/#document-rendering-suppression-for-view-transitions); or\n> - doc's [node navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#node-navigable) doesn't currently have a [rendering opportunity](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#rendering-opportunity).\n\nA document may also become render blocking while later steps happen in the procedure such as `requestAnimationFrame` callbacks. The specification should say what happens in this case when this occurs. I believe that in this case, Firefox does not update the rendering: https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/7f94689f2c228a96f6c271e30880e72778b7ab15/layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp#2637",
